From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peter Xu <peterx@redhat.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 20:00:52 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] vmstate: Implement VMS_ARRAY_OF_POINTER_AUTO_ALLOC

Backport of the following upstream commits to QEMU 10.0, needed by the
NVMe live migration support:

  f73d6251fb vmstate: Introduce vmstate_save_field_with_vmdesc()
  e86c004fbd vmstate: Allow vmstate_info_nullptr to emit non-NULL markers
  69c6d694bc vmstate: Implement load of ptr marker in vmstate core
  de62e5ba2c vmstate: Implement VMS_ARRAY_OF_POINTER_AUTO_ALLOC
  1c8784c9fd vmstate: Stop checking size for nullptr compression

Upstream builds these on top of the vmstate errp refactoring (bool
returning load/save handlers with Error **), which is not part of 10.0.
They were ported by hand onto the 10.0 int returning get/put API with
the same semantics and the same migration stream format:

  * VMS_MARKER_PTR_VALID ('1') next to VMS_MARKER_PTR_NULL ('0');
    vmstate_info_nullptr becomes vmstate_info_ptr_marker
  * VMS_ARRAY_OF_POINTER_AUTO_ALLOC: every element is prefixed with a ptr
    marker, populated elements are followed by the object and allocated
    on the destination
  * VMSTATE_VARRAY_OF_POINTER_TO_STRUCT_UINT{8,32}_ALLOC macros
  * vmstate_check() validation for the new flag

Unlike upstream, a VALID marker for a field without AUTO_ALLOC fails the
migration with an error instead of an assertion on the destination.

[ backport to QEMU 10.0 by Lierfang ]
